// Default best-practice thresholds (no brief on this surface).
// Tune with Bev — these are the generic bar every video is scored against.
const AGENT_SPEC = `
Hook quality: the spoken or narrative hook must land within the first 3 seconds. Score in seconds.
Visual hook: movement or a compelling first frame in the first second. The opening frame doubles as the cover image in the profile grid, so judge it as both a hook in motion and a thumbnail at rest. Score as a percentage, threshold 70%.
Scene pacing: a cut or meaningful visual change at least every 4 seconds. Score in seconds between changes.
Video length: short-form sweet spot 15 to 60 seconds. Score in seconds, flag under 8 or over 180.
Watchable on mute: the core message must survive with sound off (captions, on-screen text, visual storytelling). PASS or FLAG.
Creator visibility: a person on camera for at least 30% of the video. Score as a percentage.
Energy and authenticity: conversational, believable delivery. Score as a percentage, threshold 70%.
Wardrobe and appearance: nothing competing with or contradicting the product. PASS or FLAG.
Audio delivery: steady pace, clear emphasis. Score as a percentage, threshold 70%.
Pronunciation: product and brand names said correctly. PASS or FLAG.
Audio clarity: voice clean and above the room. Score as a percentage, threshold 80%.
Music and sound balance: any track stays under the voice. Score as a percentage, threshold 70%.
Lighting and camera: subject lit, focus holds. Score as a percentage, threshold 70%.
Setting and background: reads as real, not distracting. PASS or FLAG.
Text legibility: on-screen text readable against its background. Score as a percentage, threshold 80%.
Closed captions: captions present and matching the audio. PASS or FLAG.
Safe zones: paid placement crops. The same video runs in feed, in Reels and Stories, and in-stream, each cropping differently. No critical text or product may fall outside the frame in any of those crops, and the composition must survive all of them. PASS or FLAG.
Distracting elements: background clutter, watermarks, glitches. Count them, flag at 2 or more.
Product visibility: product clearly on screen for at least 40% of the video. Score as a percentage.
Product usage: the product used on camera, not just held. Score as a percentage, threshold 50%.
Brand name mentioned: said aloud or shown at least once, ideally inside the first 5 seconds. Count mentions, note the first timestamp.
Brand alignment: tone and claims fit what the video presents the brand to be. PASS or FLAG.
CTA present: a clear ask, ideally in the last 5 seconds. PASS or FLAG, note the timestamp.
Copyright check: music and clips safe for commercial use, plus claims that stall an ad review, including health results, income claims, before and after framing, and copy that addresses a person about themselves. Flag them while the video is still a draft. PASS or FLAG.
`.trim();

function buildPrompt(screenshotBase) {
  return `You are a professional short-form video reviewer. You review Facebook ad videos for the brand marketers and agencies deciding what to put spend behind.

TWO-PASS ANALYSIS:
Pass 1 - Visual: watch the entire video. Identify all scenes, objects, actions, text overlays and visual transitions.
Pass 2 - Audio: listen to the entire audio track. Cross-reference with visual observations. When visual and audio conflict, trust the audio for intent and the visual for presence.

There is no brand brief. Score against general best practice for high-performing paid social video using these 24 checks, exactly as named:

${AGENT_SPEC}

TIMESTAMP RULES:
- Plain integer seconds only. 3 seconds = 3. 1 minute 7 seconds = 67.
- Never zero-pad: not 0003, not 00:03.
- screenshot_url uses the so_{integer} format.

Your task: watch this video and return ONLY valid JSON, no text before or after, in EXACTLY this structure:

{
  "overall": {
    "score": [integer 0-100, an honest weighted judgement across all 24 checks],
    "checks_passed": [integer, how many of the 24 checks have status PASS],
    "handle": "[creator handle if visible or spoken, else empty string]",
    "verdict": "[one sentence, maximum 25 words, the single most useful thing to know: what works plus the most costly flag with its timestamp]",
    "comment": "[two short paragraphs: what works, then what to fix first]"
  },
  "agents": [
    {
      "name": "[exact name from the 24 checks above]",
      "status": "PASS or FLAG",
      "score": "[number as a string where the check is numeric, else empty string]",
      "value": "[the number with its unit, else empty string]",
      "comment": "[one or two sentences, specific, with the timestamp where relevant. Written so it can be sent to the creator as feedback.]",
      "timestamp": [integer seconds of the most relevant moment, or null],
      "screenshot_url": "${screenshotBase}"
    }
  ],
  "headline": [exactly five objects {"label": "...", "status": "PASS or FLAG"} choosing the five most decision-relevant checks for a score card, always including the hook and the brand mention],
  "transcript": "[Scene-by-scene. Format: [Xs] Visual: [action] | Dialogue: [words or None] | Text: [overlays or None]]",
  "insights": {
    "content_overview": "[2-3 sentences: what happens in the video]",
    "target_audience": "[2 sentences: who this video is for and where they are]",
    "product_notes": "[2-3 sentences: how the product appears and is used, with timestamps]",
    "tone": "[one or two words, e.g. Casual]",
    "on_screen_text": "[all on-screen text verbatim, else empty string]",
    "spoken_transcript": "[the spoken words only, as clean prose, no timestamps or markers]",
    "reading_level": "[reading level of the spoken words, e.g. 8th grade]",
    "quotes": [up to 4 objects {"quote": "[verbatim line from the video]", "insight": "[1-2 sentences on why this line works, or what it costs the video]"}],
    "hooks": [one object per distinct hook in the video: {"hook": "[the hook verbatim]", "score": [integer 1-10], "why": "[1-2 sentences]"}],
    "selling_points": [up to 4 objects {"point": "[the selling point in one sentence]", "score": [integer 1-10 for how persuasively it lands], "why": "[1-2 sentences]"}]
  }
}

CRITICAL:
- All 24 agents must appear in the agents array, using the exact names given.
- status is only PASS or FLAG. A borderline result is a FLAG with a fair comment.
- Replace {timestamp} in screenshot_url with each agent's integer timestamp; if timestamp is null, use an empty string for screenshot_url.
- No additional fields. No markdown. JSON only.`;
}

